-- The scope summary (src/col/scope_v6/): one object per scope that holds every scope key's aggregates once, instead of a copy of every fact row per key.
-- sift._test_scope_v6 builds it over a synthetic entity table, plain and over cold parts, and compares every answer with a brute force over the rows:
-- the cube of every key and month, the lookup of a key, the newest rows of a key (the ring, deletes, a filter), the dead rows taken out of a cube, the
-- pair edits (patch at read time, refresh of the keys that changed), a member of several keys, a clustered scope, coded members, a small memory budget.
-- The bytes: section tags, header and root sizes, the wide ring past 524,288 granules, the ring section LZ4-compressed when that saves 10%,
-- the month map left out for a key of one granule, the strides delta-coded and bit-packed, the compressed cube with its rollups, distinct sets and extremes,
-- the heap that picks the node to evict, the spill of month cubes under a small budget, the delta of dead rows (clean parts, the 5% rule, one granule
-- replaced alone, only the dead rows decoded, float and distinct guards), the refresh of the nodes that changed with the reclaim of their slices,
-- and the refresh after a compaction of entity parts.
-- A scope clustered by the first key of its members (a few members of several keys, a skewed key size) against the layout by member, the route of an
-- entity (SEC_SCOPE_ENT_ROUTE: one key, or several for an entity stored under more) in bytes and after a refresh, the rings of the order leaves beside
-- the time leaf (variable-length ring bytes, evictions, deletes, ties at the cut, NULLS LAST, refresh, a damaged description) for several seeds, and the rows a deletion vector and a
-- sparse IS NULL predicate take out together, the float8 extremes of a cube with NaN, infinities and signed zeros, and the month cells of a timestamptz
-- under UTC and other session zones.
-- A key that owns fewer than 32 rows of a granule has no level-0 slice (the ref says so and the rows are read when a delete asks for them), a null filter
-- on a soft-delete column leaves the soft-deleted rows out of every cube and ring (and the header says which leaf), and a scope clustered by key or by primary key
-- stays exact while members move, join and leave keys: refreshed without a rebuild, with the route of a primary-key scope still naming the keys the rows are stored under.
-- Every object a scenario opens is also asked, for every ring and both NULLS orders on a leaf that may be NULL and one that never is, which ordered reads it serves.
-- Those three run for 25 seeds.
-- Each scenario ends with failures=0.
CREATE EXTENSION pg_sift;
CREATE EXTENSION pg_sift_test;
SELECT temp_files AS temp_before FROM pg_stat_database WHERE datname = current_database() \gset
SELECT s AS scenario, l AS line
FROM unnest(ARRAY['cube', 'tstride', 'pairmap', 'build', 'lookup', 'topk', 'memory', 'robust', 'cluster', 'coded', 'delete', 'edit', 'dedupe',
	'format', 'cubewire', 'heap', 'spill', 'delta', 'refresh', 'compact', 'primary', 'route', 'rings', 'union', 'f8', 'inline', 'nullfilter', 'mapedit'])
	WITH ORDINALITY AS t(s, n),
	LATERAL regexp_split_to_table(sift._test_scope_v6(s, 1), E'\n') WITH ORDINALITY AS r(l, i)
ORDER BY n, i;
  scenario  |                                                                                            line                                                                                            
------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 cube       | cube rounds=60 exact_subtracts=4 stale_bounds=46 overflowed_dims=1
